From: win4wine
Subject: [PATCH] wineboot: do not run the StartUp folder's desktop.ini

Purpose: no Notepad with desktop.ini when the session starts after a Wine
update.
Windows behavior: the StartUp folder's desktop.ini (its localized name,
which the XP prefix writes as XP's setup does: prefix/stage.py) is the
folder's own customization, not a startup item.
Wine before: wineboot ran every file of the folder, hidden ones included, so
"wineboot -u" (prefix/stage.py after a Wine update) opened desktop.ini in
Notepad.
Change: skip desktop.ini.
Scope: every Wine prefix.
---
 programs/wineboot/wineboot.c |    3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/programs/wineboot/wineboot.c b/programs/wineboot/wineboot.c
--- a/programs/wineboot/wineboot.c
+++ b/programs/wineboot/wineboot.c
@@ -1750,6 +1750,9 @@
 	    hr = StrRetToBufW(&strret, pidlItem, wszCommand, MAX_PATH);
 	    if (FAILED(hr))
 		WINE_TRACE("Unable to parse display name.\n");
+	    /* The folder's own customization (its name and icon), as Windows skips it. */
+	    else if (!wcsicmp(PathFindFileNameW(wszCommand), L"desktop.ini"))
+		WINE_TRACE("Skipping %s.\n", wine_dbgstr_w(wszCommand));
 	    else
             {
                 HINSTANCE hinst;
